  "executive_summary": "The Docker environment hosting the ICS lab presents critical security risks due to multiple containers running with root privileges, excessive capabilities, and exposed ports. The simulation container's Docker socket mount allows full host control, while the router and PLC containers have unpatched critical vulnerabilities in kernel components and networking libraries. These weaknesses could enable attackers to manipulate ICS network configurations, execute arbitrary code in critical infrastructure components, and perform container escapes. The most dangerous attack paths involve exploiting the simulation container's Docker socket to pivot to other ICS components, or using the router's exposed port 51820/udp to compromise network segmentation. High-value assets like the PLC and simulation containers are directly exposed to these risks. The assessment was limited by the inability to verify swarm/cluster configurations due to single-node network inspection.",
